# Work on `main` except Robert’s repos (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-21), verbatim intent:

> **It was an error to develop on `local/reporting-integration`. Hard
> rule: stop using `local/reporting-integration` and stick to `main`.**

## The rule

> **AIC-owned repos under `c:\analog-pim` take new work on `main` only.
> `local/reporting-integration` and any other AIC feature branch are
> forbidden for new work. Branch only on Robert’s repos (mix-server,
> massman, pim-disc, and siblings). Never check out
> `local/reporting-integration` to continue CMMC or AIC Server work.**

## AIC repos — `main` only

Applies especially to `pim-offline-server`, `pim-offline-client`,
`pim-installers`, and `core-assets`, and to every other AIC-owned repo
in this workspace.

| Action | Required |
| --- | --- |
| New CMMC / server / client / installer / assets work | On `main` |
| Continue leftover CMMC files not already on `origin/main` | Worktree or cherry-pick **those paths only** onto `main` |
| Current branch check | `git status -sb` / `git branch --show-current` before edits |

## Forbidden

- `git checkout local/reporting-integration` (or any equivalent) to
  “continue” CMMC, PAM, or AIC Server work
- Starting or landing new AIC work on `local/reporting-integration` or
  any other AIC feature branch
- `git push --force` / `--force-with-lease` to `main` / `master`
- `git reset --hard` on the shared dirty tree
  ([`shared-working-tree-is-not-yours.mdc`](shared-working-tree-is-not-yours.mdc))

## Exception — Robert’s repos only

Feature branches are allowed **only** in Robert’s trees: `mix-server`,
`massman`, `pim-disc`, and siblings. Prefer reuse, then AIC-owned fork
when locked ([`reuse-robert-core-first.mdc`](reuse-robert-core-first.mdc),
[`fork-locked-robert-repos.mdc`](fork-locked-robert-repos.mdc)). Do not
treat that exception as permission to branch AIC Server or `core-assets`.

## Recovering leftover CMMC files

If paths exist only on `local/reporting-integration` and are **not** on
`origin/main`:

1. Stay on (or return to) `main` in the shared working tree.
2. Use a **separate worktree** or `git cherry-pick` / `git checkout
   <sha> -- <path>` for **those paths only**.
3. Stage explicit paths; commit on `main`; never `git add -A`.
4. Never force-push. Never `reset --hard`.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** Agent checks out `local/reporting-integration` to finish a
CMMC seed or server UI slice, then commits there.

**Fix:** `git switch main`. If the files are not on `origin/main`, bring
**those paths only** via worktree or cherry-pick. Leave sibling dirty
files untouched.

